  recipeId: safety
  concept: 'Authored objective: W149 Safety Recovery.

    Authored requirement:
    Disconnect, inhibit, reconnect, revalidate, reset, certify

    General teaching
    principle: Protection logic must be verified under both normal and fault conditions,
    including reset and recovery behavior.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence
    can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A safety lock must prevent unintended activation even when the normal
    switch would permit it.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Passing a normal-operation test is not proof that the protection
    system responds correctly to faults.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018W149 Safety Recovery\u2019, which component,
    reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should you inspect
    first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018W149 Safety Recovery\u2019, what result or observation would
    you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result from
    a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 107, perform the objective \u2018W149 Safety Recovery\u2019
    in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Disconnect, inhibit,
    reconnect, revalidate, reset, certify\nThe mission evaluator decides completion;
    this tutorial does not grade your answer."
